  title: Cockerel
  description: A small moulded cockerel-shaped object from the Whitechapel material
    displayed by UCL. The surviving form shows a standing bird with textured feathers
    and a broken pedestal or base. It works well as evidence for the small decorative
    and personal objects that sat alongside the tavern, household and leisure material
    from the site.
