  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  panel: {fileID: 651894516}
  title: Mallet Bottle
  description: A half-size mallet-type glass wine bottle from the Whitechapel assemblage.
    Its squat cylindrical body, long narrow neck and applied rim match the mallet
    bottle form used for storing and serving drink in the late 17th to early 18th
    century. The iridescent weathering visible on the glass is typical of archaeological
    burial conditions.
